  "answer_text": "The URL you provided\u2014`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`\u2014is a legacy address for the **Georgia Department of Revenue (DOR) Motor Vehicle Division**. \n\nThe state of Georgia has transitioned most of its online motor vehicle services to a modern portal called **Georgia DRIVES e-Services**. Old pages using the `.aspx` extension now typically redirect to this updated system.\n\n### Official Updated Links:\n* **Georgia DRIVES e-Services Portal:** [eservices.drives.ga.gov](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov/) (This is where you can complete almost all online vehicle tasks).\n* **Georgia DOR Motor Vehicle Division Homepage:** [dor.georgia.gov/motor-vehicles](https://dor.georgia.gov/motor-vehicles)\n* **Georgia License Plates & Tags Page:** [dor.georgia.gov/vehicle-registration-license-plates](https://dor.georgia.gov/vehicle-registration-license-plates)\n\n### What you can do on the Georgia DRIVES portal:\nIf you are trying to access the site to handle vehicle registration or tags, the updated system allows you to:\n* **Renew Vehicle Tags & Registrations**\n* **Look up/Reserve Prestige (Vanity) License Plates**\n* **Pre-Apply for Title and Registration** (to save time before visiting a County Tag Office)\n* **Estimate TAVT** (Title Ad Valorem Tax) or annual ad valorem tax\n* **Cancel or Reinstate Vehicle Registration**\n* **Check Title Status or Insurance Status**\n* **Pay Insurance Fines**\n\n*Note: If you have a specific, complex transaction (like registering an out-of-state vehicle for the first time), you may still need to visit your local **County Tag Office** in person.*",
